---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHead from "../../components/PageHead.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../../config/siteConfig";
const email = siteConfig.founder.email;
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | 7Captur"
  description="How 7Captur collects, uses, shares and deletes the exports, cost sheets and contact details clients and prospects give us."
  path="/privacy-policy/" current="/privacy-policy/">
<main>
<PageHead wide title="Privacy Policy" lede="How information is collected, used, shared and deleted. For how access works in practice, see the Security page." />
<section class="section section-flush" style="padding-top:48px">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="legal-layout">
      <div class="legal-toc">
        <div class="legal-toc-label">On this page</div>
        <a href="#p-who">Who we are</a>
        <a href="#p-collect">What we collect</a>
        <a href="#p-access">Access you grant</a>
        <a href="#p-use">How we use it</a>
        <a href="#p-ai">AI processing</a>
        <a href="#p-share">Who we share it with</a>
        <a href="#p-retention">Retention and deletion</a>
        <a href="#p-rights">Your rights</a>
        <a href="#p-cookies">Cookies</a>
      </div>
      <div class="legal-body">
        <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: November 2026</p>

        <h3 id="p-who">Who we are</h3>
        <p>7Captur runs a weekly profit and ad decision desk for e-commerce brands. We are the data controller for the information described here. For privacy questions, contact <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>

        <h3 id="p-collect">What we collect</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Audit and contact requests:</strong> name, work email, store URL, store platform, monthly ad spend range, active ad channels and any context you choose to add.</li>
          <li><strong>Business exports:</strong> order, refund, shipping and fee data from your store, and campaign spend and performance data from your ad accounts, as exports or through the read-only access you grant. We do not need customer names, emails or addresses and ask you not to send them.</li>
          <li><strong>Cost sheets:</strong> the SKU cost files you upload, and the payment fee and refund-window notes you provide.</li>
          <li><strong>Client portal:</strong> for invited clients, your name, email address, sign-in details handled by our authentication provider, delivery preferences (email addresses, an optional Slack webhook URL, delivery day, time and time zone) and the memos and invoices shown to you.</li>
          <li><strong>Billing records:</strong> invoice numbers, periods, amounts and payment status. We invoice directly, and we do not hold card numbers on this site.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 id="p-access">Access you grant</h3>
        <p>We work through the native view-only roles your platforms provide: a Shopify staff account with reports and orders view access, an ad account analyst role in Meta Business Manager, and a read-only user in Google Ads. We do not ask you to install a third-party app, authorize an OAuth connection, change a pixel or give us billing or edit access. You can remove any role at any time, and our access ends when you do.</p>

        <h3 id="p-use">How we use it</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>To produce your audit and weekly decision memos, and to answer your questions about them.</li>
          <li>To deliver memos by email, Slack or the client portal, to invoice you and to provide support.</li>
          <li>To secure accounts, prevent abuse and keep the service reliable.</li>
          <li>We do not sell your data, we do not share it for anyone's marketing, and we do not benchmark one client's records against another's.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 id="p-ai">AI processing</h3>
        <p>Our own code reconciles your numbers and a human analyst verifies every call before it reaches you. We may use an AI service to help draft plain-language wording and to answer questions about a client's current report data. We do not use client financial records to train public models.</p>

        <h3 id="p-share">Who we share it with</h3>
        <p>We use service providers to run 7Captur: cloud hosting, database and file storage (Google Cloud and Firebase), email delivery, form handling (Formspree), call scheduling, and an AI service as described above. They process data on our instructions. If you choose Slack delivery, memo summaries are posted to the webhook you provide. We may disclose information if the law requires it.</p>

        <h3 id="p-retention">Retention and deletion</h3>
        <p>We keep your exports, cost sheets and memos while we work together. On request, we delete all stored exports and memos within 48 hours and confirm the deletion in writing. Invoice and payment records may be kept for as long as accounting and legal rules require.</p>

        <h3 id="p-rights">Your rights</h3>
        <p>You can ask to access, correct, export or delete the personal data we hold about you, and to withdraw consent where we rely on it. Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>

        <h3 id="p-cookies">Cookies</h3>
        <p>This website uses no tracking cookies, third-party analytics scripts or advertising pixels. Your browser stores only your light or dark theme choice, and your cookie notice choice.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</main>
</Layout>
